This folder contains unique hardware configurations used in the SE performance tests.

It contains sub-folders for performance experiments, where the configuration may be changed
for any run, and performance regressions, where the configuration is expected to be immutable
for its lifetime.

Each hardware configuration is known by it's unique file name. It is very important that
this filename not change once it has been used, as this filename gets saved with the
performance results and will be used in queries to filter and return particular
performance data.

The naming convention used is trying to clearly identify the main parameters of the
hardware configuration, being instance type and number of nodes. This is more useful
and reusable than a naming convention of the purpose of the config file. e.g. It is
more useful to have file named r5dn.16xlarge-6N.config than one named tpch-sf1000.config
as the former could be reused for other purposes whereas a user needs to open the latter
and look at its contents to get more information.

Please think carefully about how hardware configs are named as they are saved in the
database with their configuration to guard against the case where a regular repeating
hardware config is unknowingly changed in such a way that the results of other jobs using
it are affected. We need to ensure that configurations are consistent and hence they should
be treated as being immutable.